-- title:
--   Sections near an adic point as quotients of integral sections
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal X_C$ denotes the scheme `Limits.pullback f sC`, i.e. the fibre product of $f:\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $sC:\operatorname{Spec}C\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, with projections $p_1=$ `Limits.pullback.fst f sC` and $p_2=$ `Limits.pullback.snd f sC`.
--
--   **Arithmetic base.** Fixed are a prime $r$; a characteristic-zero commutative domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi\in\mathcal O$, with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); and a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficients.** A characteristic-zero commutative domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every $x\in Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo it (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo it (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo it for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Determinant valuation.** A homomorphism $v\!\det:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) such that $v\!\det(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Group data.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma:G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma\le G$ such that some $z\in\Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix $c\cdot 1$ with $v\!\det(\sigma z)=2$ (`hcent`), some $w\in\Gamma$ has $v\!\det(\sigma w)=1$ (`hodd`), and a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by $x\in\Gamma'\iff x\in\Gamma$ and $v\!\det(\sigma x)$ even (`hΓ'`). Further, a homomorphism $\rho:G\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with $\rho g$ the class of $\sigma g$ (`hρ`), such that every vertex $v$ of the lattice tree [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪 K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) has finite stabiliser in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hdisc`) and some finite set $S$ of vertices meets every $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit (`hcocpt`).
--
--   **The quotient datum.** A scheme $\mathcal X$ (in universe $0$) and a proper flat morphism $f:\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, together with a family $\Theta$ which, for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, maps pairs $(\psi,P)$ with $\psi:Onr\to_{\mathcal O} B$ and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ — that is, an element of `(Omega K₀ π).obj B`: an assignment to each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M\subset K_0^2$ of a $B$-submodule $\mathrm{line}(M)\subseteq B\otimes_{\mathcal O}M$ with invertible quotient, monotone under lattice inclusions, equivariant for homotheties, and satisfying the nondegeneracy condition of `DeligneDatum` at every prime of $B$ — to elements of `(Scheme.nilpPoints f).obj B`, i.e. to morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal X$ lifting $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. Four hypotheses constrain $\Theta$. `hΘnat`: $\Theta$ is natural in $B$ for $\mathcal O$-algebra maps. `hΘinv`: $\Theta$ is invariant under the twisted $\Gamma$-action, i.e. if $\gamma\in\Gamma$ and `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B (σ γ) x x'` holds — meaning $x'_1=x_1\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $x'_2$ is the pullback of $x_2$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback` — then $\Theta(x')=\Theta(x)$. `hΘfib`: for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi:Onr\to_{\mathcal O}k$, the map $P\mapsto\Theta\,(\psi,P)$ is onto `(Scheme.nilpPoints f).obj k`, and $\Theta(\psi,P)=\Theta(\psi,P')$ holds precisely when some $\gamma\in\Gamma$ satisfies `IsTwistedAct` for $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$. `hΘuniv`: $\Theta$ is initial among such data — for every scheme $T$ with $t:T\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and every family $\rho'$ into `Scheme.nilpPoints t` that is natural in $B$ and twisted-$\Gamma$-invariant in the above sense, there is a family $u$ from `Scheme.nilpPoints f` to `Scheme.nilpPoints t`, natural in $B$, with $u\circ\Theta=\rho'$, and any natural $u'$ with $u'\circ\Theta=\rho'$ agrees with $u$ at every $B$ and every point.
--
--   **Analytic frame.** A field $C$ with a $K_0$-algebra structure, a valuation `Valued C Γ₀` with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero, complete and algebraically closed; a commutative ring $R$ with compatible $\mathcal O$- and $C$-algebra structures (scalar towers $\mathcal O\to R\to C$ and $\mathcal O\to K_0\to C$); a pseudo-uniformizer $\varpi$, that is an element of $K_0$ whose image in $C$ has valuation strictly between $0$ and $1$ and whose powers bound the valuation of every nonzero element of $K_0$ from both sides; and `hF : IsAdicFrame π ϖ R`, which asserts that $\pi$ is irreducible, $R\to C$ is injective with image exactly the elements of valuation $\le 1$, $R$ is $\pi$-adically complete, $\mathcal O$ is exactly the set of elements of $K_0$ of valuation $\le 1$, the image of $K_0$ is closed in $C$, and $\pi$ and $\varpi$ have the same image in $C$. Further: an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi_0:Onr\to R$; `hrk`, that for $x,y\in C$ with $v(x)<1$ and $y\ne0$ some power $v(x)^n\le v(y)$; `hval`, that every nonzero $\varepsilon\in\Gamma_0$ is $\ge v(y)$ for some nonzero $y\in C$; `hex : Omega.IsExhausted ϖ`, that every element of $C$ outside the image of $K_0$ lies in one of the affinoids `affinoid ϖ n`; and the assumption that the ring `Omega.HolRingOf ϖ ρ` of functions on the Drinfeld upper half plane holomorphic on every such affinoid is a domain.
--
--   **Uniformisation of adic points.** A map $\Phi$ from `AdicPoint K₀ π R` — compatible systems of Deligne data over the rings $R/(\pi^{n+1})$ — to the set of morphisms $p:\operatorname{Spec}R\to\mathcal X$ with $p$ followed by $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O\to R)$, subject to `hΦ`, a conjunction of four clauses: (a) for every adic point $x$ and every $n$, $\operatorname{Spec}(R\to R/(\pi^{n+1}))$ followed by $\Phi x$ equals the morphism underlying $\Theta$ applied over $R/(\pi^{n+1})$ to the pair consisting of $\psi_0$ reduced modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ and the $n$-th level $x.\mathrm{pt}\,n$; (b) $\Phi$ is surjective; (c) $\Phi x=\Phi x'$ if and only if $x'=x.\mathrm{act}(\sigma\gamma)$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma'$; (d) base change along $R\to C$ is injective on such $R$-points, and every $C$-point $\operatorname{Spec}C\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ is the base change of one of them.
--
--   **Generic fibre.** The morphism $sC$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O\to K_0\to C$ (`hsC`), and $\mathcal X_C$ is assumed integral, so it has a generic point $\eta$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every open $U\subseteq\mathcal X_C$ with $\eta\in U$, every section $s\in\Gamma(U,\mathcal O_{\mathcal X_C})$, every adic point $x$ and every morphism $q:\operatorname{Spec}C\to\mathcal X_C$ such that $q$ followed by $p_1$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(R\to C)$ followed by $\Phi x$, and $q$ followed by $p_2$ is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec}C$, there exist an open $V\subseteq\mathcal X$ with $(\Phi x)^{-1}V=\top$ (so $\Phi x$ factors through $V$), an open $W\subseteq\mathcal X_C$ with $W\le p_1^{-1}V$, $q^{-1}W=\top$ and $\eta\in W$, and natural numbers $m,m'$ with families $\mathrm{num}:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\Gamma(V,\mathcal O_{\mathcal X})$, $c_{\mathrm{num}}:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to C$, $\mathrm{den}:\mathrm{Fin}\,m'\to\Gamma(V,\mathcal O_{\mathcal X})$, $c_{\mathrm{den}}:\mathrm{Fin}\,m'\to C$, for which the following three assertions hold. Write
--   $$D=\sum_j \langle c_{\mathrm{den}}\,j\rangle|_W\cdot\bigl(p_1^{\#}(\mathrm{den}\,j)\bigr)|_W,\qquad N=\sum_i \langle c_{\mathrm{num}}\,i\rangle|_W\cdot\bigl(p_1^{\#}(\mathrm{num}\,i)\bigr)|_W$$
--   in $\Gamma(W,\mathcal O_{\mathcal X_C})$, where $\langle c\rangle$ is the global section of $\mathcal X_C$ obtained from $c\in C$ through the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso` followed by the map on global sections induced by $p_2$, restricted to $W$, and $p_1^{\#}:\Gamma(V,\mathcal O_{\mathcal X})\to\Gamma(p_1^{-1}V,\mathcal O_{\mathcal X_C})$ is the comparison map of $p_1$ at $V$, its values again restricted to $W$.
--
--   (i) $D\neq 0$.
--
--   (ii) On $W\cap U$ the restriction of $s$ times the restriction of $D$ equals the restriction of $N$; that is, $s\cdot D=N$ after restricting all three along $W\cap U\le U$ respectively $W\cap U\le W$.
--
--   (iii) If moreover $q$ factors through $U$ (i.e. $q^{-1}U=\top$), then there are an open $W'\le W$ with $q^{-1}W'=\top$ such that the restriction of $D$ to $W'$ is a unit in $\Gamma(W',\mathcal O_{\mathcal X_C})$.
--
--   This is the local presentation step underlying the evaluation of rational functions on the generic fibre $\mathcal X_C$ of a Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient at the $C$-points coming from adic points of the formal upper half plane: an arbitrary section near the generic point is exhibited, on a neighbourhood of both the generic point and the given $C$-point, as a quotient $N/D$ of finite $C$-linear combinations of sections pulled back from $\mathcal X$, with $D$ nonzero and invertible at the point whenever the point lies in the domain of the section. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_invariant_chartwiseMeromorphic_pullback_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient_of_eval_of_smooth`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_invariant_chartwiseMeromorphic_pullback_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient_of_eval_of_smooth) and by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_invariantFieldOf_eval_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient_of_smooth`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_invariantFieldOf_eval_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient_of_smooth), and relies on the affineness of $p_1^{-1}V$ over an affine open $V$ together with the description of its sections as finite sums, as recorded in [`AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_preimage_fst_and_exists_eq_sum_of_isAffineOpen`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_preimage_fst_and_exists_eq_sum_of_isAffineOpen).
